<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Thomas Hobbes</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1588–1679</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Thomas Hobbes was an English philosopher whose <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/leviathan">Leviathan</a> of 1651 is a founding work of modern political thought. Writing during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/english-civil-war">English Civil War</a>, he argued that without a sovereign power life would be a war of all against all, and that people agree to a social contract giving authority to a ruler to secure peace. He also wrote on geometry, physics and the nature of human beings.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thomas-hobbes.jpg" alt="Thomas Hobbes" width="320" height="424" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: John Michael Wright · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Thomas_Hobbes_by_John_Michael_Wright_(colour)_(3x4_cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
